# The Falco pin and the kernel range it is known to run on (Story 10.1).
# ONE place: deploy/helm/falco_pin_test.go fails the build if the chart, the
# support matrix or preflight disagree with it.
#
# Why an RC: Falco 0.43.1 and 0.44.x exit every few minutes on kernel 7.x
# ("could not parse param ... type 223 (clone)" / "type 307 (openat)"),
# falcosecurity/falco#3955. The modern_bpf per-CPU auxmap is overwritten when a
# BPF program is preempted on PREEMPT_DYNAMIC kernels (falcosecurity/libs#2719),
# fixed by falcosecurity/libs#3086 (merged 2026-09-08), first shipped in libs
# 0.26.0-rc1 and therefore Falco 0.45.0-rc1 (2026-09-09).
# TODO(#103 follow-up): move to 0.45.0 GA when it ships (milestone 0.45.0,
# planned 2026-09-21) and bump FALCO_CHART_VERSION to the chart that ships it.

# falcosecurity/falco Helm chart version (Chart.yaml dependency).
FALCO_CHART_VERSION=9.1.0
# Falco image tag the chart pins (values.yaml falco.image.tag).
FALCO_PINNED_VERSION=0.45.0-rc1
# First Falco release with the libs#3086 fix. Below it, kernel >= 7.0 crashes.
FALCO_PREEMPT_FIX_VERSION=0.45.0
# modern_ebpf needs BTF and the BPF ring buffer: "usually all versions >=5.8
# are enough", though some distributions backport them (Falco kernel docs).
FALCO_MIN_KERNEL=5.8
# Newest kernel series this pin has been soaked on (30 min, 0 restarts).
FALCO_MAX_TESTED_KERNEL=7.0
